# Plan part F10 (proposed ADR-0443, INV-0443-5), the positive control of top.script's room. The
# limit (@LIMIT@) is what `tools/room-mid-limit.py` computes from top.script's log: the room's
# reading with `t_shared keep` and its launcher alone (P0), less half of what an image keeps. A
# room of that size holds everything the program needs except half of its image: the program
# starts only if its image is NOT charged to the room. With the image charged to the room (the
# shell naming the room's job) the program is refused and the shell says the room is at its memory limit; with
# the shell naming its own job it prints "L alone" and the `!` line below fails the script.
! panicked
! ZORAYA-PANIC
! t_shared: keep: L alone
< \r\n~> 
> room new mid --mem @LIMIT@ --procs 16 +w /work\r
< mid --colour
< \r\n~> 
> room mid\r
< mid /work> 
> /bin/t_shared keep &\r
< mid /work> 
> sleep 5\r
< mid /work> 
> top mid\r
< room mid is at its memory limit
< mid /work> 
> room --leave\r
< \r\n/work> 
> room remove mid --kill\r
< \r\n/work> 
> poweroff\r
